# Build context for `docker build .` (see Dockerfile).
#
# Two rules decide what is listed here:
#   1. Never send the host's build artifacts into the image. `web/dist` and `sidecar/dist` are rebuilt
#      inside their own stages; a stale host bundle copied in by `COPY . .` would silently ship.
#   2. Never send state or secrets into a layer. `data/` holds a development SQLite database (with real
#      rows) and `.env` holds secrets; both would be baked into the image history.
#
# Anything not matched here reaches the Go stage's `COPY . .`, which is why this file lists directories
# rather than trying to allowlist sources.

.git
.github
.opencode
.env
.env.*

bin/
data/
backups/
doc/

web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/dist.new/
sidecar/node_modules/
sidecar/dist/

*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.tsbuildinfo
